    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "046cfc45_59caa5fd",
        "filename": "service-t/src/com/android/server/NsdService.java",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 419,
      "author": {
        "id": 1288034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-16T06:35:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There\u0027s a bit more validation to do here I think; the original implementation used ConstructServiceName: http://go/aocs/android/platform/superproject/+/master:external/mdnsresponder/mDNSCore/mDNS.c;drc\u003d9f75a97cc42ff34708ea59ba7904164739deca91;l\u003d8763\n\nFrom what read of that function, I think the type must match the regex:\n\n    ^(_[a-zA-Z0-9-_]{1,62}[a-zA-Z0-9]\\.)?(_[a-zA-Z0-9-_]{1,62}[a-zA-Z0-9]\\._(?:tcp|udp))$\n\n(optional subtype, then type, then _tcp or _udp. Types and subtype must be 1-63 characters with a leading underscore, and must not end with dashes or underscores).\n\nAnd if the first capture group matches something, it should actually discover for match.group(1) + \"_sub.\" + match.group(2)\n\nI\u0027ve written a test in aosp/2388109 to help validate",
      "revId": "39637d9251919c2c74727b20abe2315ce56da5bf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
